{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Morning. In about the ankles, is it?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Swollen ankles.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Three weeks.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sore?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): What do they feel like?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): My feet feel dead.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Energy?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): I feel like a wet rag.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any cough?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): A frog in my throat.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Passing water often?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Up at night?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Twice.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): The chart has the amlodopine at five milligrams, uh, how long on it?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Ten. Five-ish years.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Bendroflumethazide two point five each morning?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): Taking them every day?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Mostly.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Still for the blood pressure?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Short of breath?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Here today you're 158 over 96. What was it at home?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): One thirty two over eighty.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Was the house quiet for that?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): I can't hear myself think.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): And a lot of walking?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): I've overdone it.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Grand so, both ankles pit. I'd say the amlodipine is doing the swelling and the water tablet has you running to the loo. I'll stop the amlodipine, start ramipril five milligrams every morning, get the kidney bloods booked, and see you in a fortnight. Keep the feet up in the evenings."
 ],
